WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Keep organization and workspace settings distinct. Organization settings manage the name and logo. A workspace groups records, configuration and access.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Edit the organization identity. The name and logo apply across its workspaces. This demonstration cancels the edit without making changes.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Choose the intended organization. Organizations are separate access and ownership contexts. Check the selected one before creating a workspace.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Create a workspace within that organization. Enter a recognizable name. This walkthrough previews the form and cancels; it does not create another workspace.

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Inspect the workspace record. Open a row to confirm its name, organization and access status. New workspaces start with Sandbox access.

6
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Review product availability. Products shows Insights and Signal for the selected environment. Access does not itself run underwriting or monitoring.

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Trace administrative changes in Audit log. Open an event to inspect its action, actor, target and recorded metadata.

8
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Use identifiers to keep the scope clear. Organization and workspace identifiers are different. Invite teammates from the workspace they need to access.
